;; A WORKED EXAMPLE shipped with the seed — not a configuration. Copy the one
;; matching your seat to resources/profile.edn and edit it.
;;
;; SEAT :agy-ide — the Antigravity IDE's CLI. Its sibling is claude.edn, and the
;; pair is instructive: they are near mirror images. Here Google writes and
;; Anthropic reviews; there Anthropic writes and Google reviews. Between them
;; both tool-call adapters are exercised, which is why there are two rather
;; than one.
;;
;; Model names are dated selections (decision log P0-3: "Specific models are
;; dated selections"). The SHAPE is the part meant to outlive them.
;;
;; Three things this file is careful about:
;;
;;   ONE SEAT. The interactive client is where the human sits. The three
;;   dispatched roles are reached over HTTP by the harness and are not anyone's
;;   editor — so there is exactly one :seat, and it is a scalar so it cannot
;;   grow a second. :seat names a tool `bb doctor` knows how to probe.
;;
;;   THE CODER'S FAMILY FOLLOWS THE SEAT, by convention and not by rule. The
;;   seat here is a Google client, so the Coder is Gemini and Anthropic moves to
;;   the verifying side — the exact reverse of claude.edn. It is not checked,
;;   because OpenCode 2 and Pi are bring-your-own-model clients with no inherent
;;   family: the relation is not expressible for half the seats this kit
;;   supports.
;;
;;   VERIFIER ≠ CODER FAMILY. Method §05 and decision log P0-3, and this one IS
;;   checked. The Tester and the Reviewer both verify the Coder, so neither may
;;   share its family. `bb profile` is the only place that rule has ever been
;;   anything but prose.
;;
;;   NO KEYS, EVER. :key-env NAMES an environment variable. This file is
;;   committed; a field that could hold a secret would eventually be handed one.

{:seat :agy-ide

 :roles
 {:coder {:family :google
          :model "google/gemini-3.8-flash"
          :shape :openai
          :endpoint "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
          :key-env "OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
          ;; Pinned request-side: without :allow_fallbacks false, the provider
          ;; you logged yesterday is not the one you get today, and a different
          ;; provider can mean a different chat template.
          ;; MEDIUM, NOT HIGH, AND THAT IS MEASURED. The original sketch put
          ;; :reasoning_effort "high" on every OpenRouter role, unexamined. On
          ;; gemini-3.8-flash as Reviewer it produced 27,706 tokens, 4m09s and an
          ;; EMPTY final message; the identical dispatch at medium answered in 63s
          ;; for half the money with real findings. High reasoning on a flash tier
          ;; spends the budget thinking and has nothing left to say with — D1 saw
          ;; the same shape when a small max_tokens returned empty content.
          :params {:reasoning_effort "medium"
                   :provider {:only ["google-vertex"] :allow_fallbacks false}}}

  ;; CHOOSE THE TESTER BY ITS TESTS, NOT ITS PRICE — see claude.edn for run
  ;; D4, which established it, and bake-off B1, which chose this model on
  ;; exactly those terms. Same Tester as that profile: the result does not
  ;; depend on the seat, and openai is neither Coder's family. The standard
  ;; endpoint rather than flex, because flex was rate-limited upstream on most
  ;; requests when this was switched; claude.edn has the numbers, and why the
  ;; "openai" pin is observed rather than guaranteed to mean standard.
  :tester {:family :openai
           :model "openai/gpt-5.6-sol"
           :shape :openai
           :endpoint "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1"
           :key-env "OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
           :params {:reasoning_effort "medium"
                    :provider {:only ["openai"] :allow_fallbacks false}}}

  ;; Direct to Anthropic, which is the :anthropic tool-call shape. No
  ;; :provider pin: that endpoint does no routing, so there is nothing to pin.
  ;;
  ;; CLAUDE FABLE 5.1 AT LOW EFFORT, replacing claude-sonnet-5 (2026-09-14).
  ;; The same settings as claude.edn's Coder, for the reasons given there:
  ;; thinking counts against :max_tokens, no fallback model answers a refusal,
  ;; and the cost is computed from :pricing because the endpoint reports none.
  ;; Chosen on the user's judgement, not a run: no Anthropic model has yet been
  ;; dispatched as Reviewer (DEVLOG.md, 2026-09-14 17:19).
  :reviewer {:family :anthropic
             :model "claude-fable-5-1"
             :shape :anthropic
             :endpoint "https://api.anthropic.com"
             :key-env "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"
             :params {:output_config {:effort "low"}
                      :max_tokens 16000}
             ;; USD per million tokens: base input, output, 5-minute and 1-hour
             ;; cache writes, cache reads (0.025x on Fable 5.1; 0.1x elsewhere).
             :pricing {:per-mtok {:in 10 :out 50
                                  :cache-write-5m 12.5 :cache-write-1h 20
                                  :cache-read 0.25}
                       :source "https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/pricing"
                       :as-of "2026-09-14"}}}}
